# Project Structure

This project follows **Vertical Slice Architecture** – organize by features, not technical layers.

## Core Principles

- **Features over layers** – each feature is self-contained
- **Colocate by use case** – everything a feature needs lives together
- **No global god-objects** – no shared `services/`, `models/`, `utils/` folders
- **Feature independence** – features don't depend on each other (use Facades for orchestration)

## Feature Structure (Vertical Slice)

```text
/feature-name/                    # Fachliche Feature (z.B. user-management)
  /+state/                        # State Management
    /models/                      # Domain Models & DTOs
      user.interface.ts
      user-dto.ts
      index.ts
    /configs/                     # Entity Configs
      user.config.ts
    /features/                    # SignalStore Features
      user-entities.feature.ts    # Entity Feature (Aggregate)
      user-actions.feature.ts     # Actions Feature (Commands)
    /facades/                     # Orchestration (optional)
      user-management.facade.ts
    feature.store.ts              # Root Store
    index.ts
  /services/                      # HTTP Services (Repositories)
    user.service.ts
  /components/                    # Feature Components
    /user-list/
      /+store/                    # UI Sub-Store (optional)
        user-list-ui.store.ts
      user-list.component.ts
      user-list.component.html
      user-list.component.scss
  /constants/                     # Feature Constants
    api-endpoints.ts
  /helpers/                       # Feature Utilities
    user-utils.ts
  /pipes/                         # Feature Pipes
  /directives/                    # Feature Directives
  index.ts                        # Public API
```

## Store Organization

```text
/+state/
  /models/              # Domain & DTOs
  /configs/             # Entity Configs
  /features/            # Reusable SignalStore Features
    entities.feature.ts
    actions.feature.ts
    ui.feature.ts
  /facades/             # Orchestration Stores
    feature.facade.ts
  feature.store.ts      # Root Feature Store
```

## Core Folder (Cross-Cutting Concerns)

```text
/core/
  /models/              # Shared interfaces (BaseResponse, etc.)
  /helpers/             # Shared utilities (http-error-utils, etc.)
  /guards/              # Route guards
  /interceptors/        # HTTP interceptors
  /pipes/               # Global pipes
  /directives/          # Global directives
  /constants/           # Global constants
  index.ts
```

## API Endpoints (Feature-Scoped)

Keep API endpoints within features:

```ts
// ✅ GOOD - Feature-scoped
// user-management/constants/api-endpoints.ts
export const API_USER_ENDPOINTS = {
  users: 'users',
  activeUsers: 'users/active',
} as const;

// ❌ BAD - Global god-object
// constants/api-endpoints.ts
export const API_ENDPOINTS = {
  users: 'users',
  orders: 'orders',
  products: 'products',
  // ... 500 more endpoints
};
```

## Example: Complete Feature Layout

```text
/user-management/
  /+state/
    /models/
      user.interface.ts
      user-dto.ts
      index.ts
    /configs/
      user.config.ts
    /features/
      user-entities.feature.ts      # withUserEntities()
      user-actions.feature.ts       # withUserActions()
    user-management.store.ts        # Root Store
    index.ts
  /services/
    user.service.ts                 # Pure HTTP adapter
  /components/
    /user-list/
      /+store/
        user-list-ui.store.ts       # Component-scoped UI store
      user-list.component.ts
      user-list.component.html
      user-list.component.scss
    /user-detail/
      user-detail.component.ts
  /constants/
    api-endpoints.ts
  /helpers/
    user-utils.ts
  index.ts                          # Public API of feature
```

## Import Rules

### ✅ Allowed

- Feature → Core (shared utilities)
- Component → Feature Store
- Store → Service (same feature)
- Facade → Multiple Stores

### ❌ Forbidden

- Feature → Feature (direct import)
- Service → Service
- Store → Store (without Facade)
- Component → Service (direct HTTP)

## Public API (index.ts)

Each feature exports a public API:

```ts
// user-management/index.ts
export * from './+state/user-management.store';
export * from './+state/models';
export { UserService } from './services/user.service';

// Don't export internals:
// ❌ export * from './+state/features/...';
// ❌ export * from './helpers/...';
```

## Refactoring Benefits

With Vertical Slices:

- Delete feature = delete folder
- No "dead code archaeology"
- Clear feature boundaries
- Easy to move/split features
- No implicit coupling
